I mean, you wouldn't do
anything really cool, would you?

264
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:15,740
Like not feed us?

265
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:18,350
Attention!

266
00:13:18,433 --> 00:13:19,752
Training will now begin!

267
00:13:22,180 --> 00:13:24,217
Why do you want to find a crest, Izzy?

268
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:27,124
I guess it's mostly just
because of Kabuterimon.

269
00:13:27,300 --> 00:13:31,077
I would like to see what stage he
will digivolve into after that one.

270
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:33,637
Isn't that the reason why
you're looking for a crest?

271
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:34,550
No.

272
00:13:34,633 --> 00:13:37,860
I want to use the crest
to digivolve me. Oh?

273
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:41,277
Not into a Digimon, but to
make me stronger and smarter.

274
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:45,157
Maybe learn something new about myself,
you know, to reach my next level.

275
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:46,070
Mm-hmm.

276
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,900
The barrier of this land.

277
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:51,297
Don't tell me we came
all this way for nothing.

278
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:52,792
Wait, look at that glow.

279
00:13:53,860 --> 00:13:55,557
We made it! The crests!

280
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:58,197
The crests have got to be
right there inside the well.

281
00:13:58,280 --> 00:13:59,110
Let's go!

282
00:13:59,193 --> 00:14:00,982
Yeah, but it's outside the wall.

283
00:14:01,100 --> 00:14:03,400
I know, but we're so close.

284
00:14:08,580 --> 00:14:10,109
Hope my hand doesn't melt.

285
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:15,620
It's okay, Matt.

286
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:16,657
We can go through it.

287
00:14:16,740 --> 00:14:17,570
Yeah.

288
00:14:23,540 --> 00:14:24,400
Say anything?

289
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:27,300
The light's bright down here.

290
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:31,177
Hey, we should try holding
our tags up towards the wall.

291
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:32,090
Good call.

292
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:36,350
Wow.

293
00:14:37,900 --> 00:14:39,860
Izzy, man, this is happening.

294
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:41,760
We both found our crests.

295
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:49,660
Edermon, we have contact
in sector G3, sir. What?

296
00:14:49,980 --> 00:14:51,797
Well, that's the sector
we just passed through.

297
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:54,757
Turn us around, turn us around,
you little whippersnapper.

298
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:55,917
What are you waiting for?

299
00:14:58,780 --> 00:14:59,610
Send him at once.

300
00:14:59,693 --> 00:15:01,776
I love a roadie with a good appetite.

301
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:11,230
Tyranomon,

302
00:15:11,313 --> 00:15:16,140
a huge Digimon with fire breath strong
enough to cook a couple of boys like you.

303
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:32,480
No, Gavuman!

304
00:15:32,780 --> 00:15:35,237
Making funny faces will
not defeat your enemies!

305
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:36,257
You must always...

306
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:37,170
Huh?

307
00:15:37,253 --> 00:15:38,328
My barrier has been broken!

308
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:39,350
Oh, Izzy's there!

309
00:15:39,433 --> 00:15:41,300
He might be in trouble! And Matt!

310
00:15:41,520 --> 00:15:42,873
We've got to help them!

311
00:15:48,060 --> 00:15:50,217
Didn't I see this guy
in one of my nightmares?

312
00:15:50,300 --> 00:15:53,006
I wish you'd be more
careful what you'd dream.

313
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:54,640
Matt, Izzy, over here.

314
00:15:54,880 --> 00:15:57,080
Thank goodness you're safe. Hey, bro.

315
00:15:58,200 --> 00:16:00,200
Well, well, well, isn't that nice?

316
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:02,106
Everybody's all together now.

317
00:16:02,380 --> 00:16:06,027
You know I can't resist an
audience, so I guess it's showtime.

318
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:12,840
Here's this song I call
Bye-Bye, Digimon, Bye-Bye.

319
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:16,840
My power's been drained.

320
00:16:18,480 --> 00:16:21,560
It zapped them, so now
they can't digivolve.

321
00:16:25,740 --> 00:16:27,020
It's no use.

322
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:30,064
The more we fight it, the
farther away we drift.

323
00:16:55,940 --> 00:16:58,360
I remember this bridge.

324
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:15,160
What is it? Who's that?

325
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:18,950
Me.

326
00:17:19,033 --> 00:17:19,920
But I...

327
00:17:20,940 --> 00:17:22,040
What? That's you?

328
00:17:25,140 --> 00:17:27,260
Tai! Ugly man! What are you doing?

329
00:17:27,480 --> 00:17:28,857
Your friends have been in trouble!

330
00:17:28,940 --> 00:17:30,777
You've got to come back
before it's too late!

331
00:17:30,860 --> 00:17:31,690
Tai!

332
00:17:31,773 --> 00:17:32,603
Can you hear me?

333
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:38,680
I'm never gonna learn how to
ride my bike. Don't give up.

334
00:17:38,780 --> 00:17:42,117
You can't call it quits now just
because of one or two mistakes you made.

335
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:44,729
Man, I've made plenty,
and I ought to know.

336
00:17:45,220 --> 00:17:48,120
You just have to get up
and try again. Uh-huh.

337
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:49,940
Okay, I'll try.

338
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:53,860
We can hold you up from behind.

339
00:17:59,340 --> 00:18:01,780
See? You're doing it. You're doing great.

340
00:18:03,260 --> 00:18:06,000
Hey, I'm doing it all
by myself. I'm riding.

341
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:08,260
Wait, Agumon, I get it.

342
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:10,257
It's all about overcoming your fear.

343
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:13,997
I was so afraid of you digivolving
back into Skull Greymon

344
00:18:14,080 --> 00:18:18,777
again That I lost it You must
be a mind reader That same fear

345
00:18:18,860 --> 00:18:22,477
stopped me from digivolving
to Greymon But if we really

346
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:26,940
believe in ourselves It'll be
just like riding a bike Greymon,

347
00:18:27,100 --> 00:18:29,041
my friend, I'm coming back to you

348
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:36,260
We're on our way back Right, together

349
00:18:45,680 --> 00:18:48,520
Oh, they're in real trouble. Woo-hoo!

350
00:19:05,660 --> 00:19:07,617
Can't wait for Tai any longer.

351
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:10,440
He needs this lesson,
but I've got to attack!

352
00:19:12,700 --> 00:19:13,620
Agumon!

353
00:19:13,900 --> 00:19:14,820
Digivolve!

354
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:18,000
Raymon!

355
00:19:25,860 --> 00:19:27,600
Hey, he digivolved!

356
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:30,700
Nova Browse!

357
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:39,040
You made it! Yeah.

358
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:42,221
Grandma's pulling the cables out.

359
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:46,680
Get him, Grandma! Go, go!

360
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:04,390
He did it!

361
00:20:04,540 --> 00:20:05,500
Greymon did it!

362
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:08,759
Look at the black cables
all shattering into pieces!

363
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:18,977
Well, they cut it kind of
close, but they did it.

364
00:20:19,060 --> 00:20:19,890
Yep, yep.

365
00:20:19,973 --> 00:20:21,657
Those rod kids made me a gay and all.

366
00:20:21,740 --> 00:20:25,157
I gotta find something easier to beat
like some cardboard boxes or something.

367
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:26,317
Thank you, Pixiemon.

368
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:27,777
We've learned a lot from you.

369
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:30,597
Yeah, like how to scrub floors
and starve half to death.

370
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:31,510
Joe?

371
00:20:31,593 --> 00:20:32,997
That's just Joe's stomach talking.

372
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:34,904
Far from over your training is.

373
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:37,417
Remember, life itself
is a training session.

374
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:39,240
Learn all you can. Right!

375
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:44,680
They truly are the Digi-Destiny. Yep, yep.

376
00:20:44,940 --> 00:20:47,897
No doubt have I, for though
they are sometimes foolish,

377
00:20:47,980 --> 00:20:49,877
I have seen the love in their hearts.

378
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:54,140
With a little luck, they just may
succeed and save our digital world.

379
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:27,940
I wish, how are you here?

380
00:21:57,940 --> 00:22:02,880
When I see my eyes, I'll
remind you of the day.

381
00:22:05,300 --> 00:22:10,320
That day, that time, I'll see a dream.

382
00:22:12,860 --> 00:22:16,100
When I see the wind, I'll see the day.

383
00:22:17,020 --> 00:22:21,480
I can't see the future.

384
00:22:24,700 --> 00:22:25,657
I'm sure, I'm sure,

385
00:22:51,480 --> 00:22:52,637
Now, we're going to go
through the machine.

386
00:22:52,720 --> 00:22:55,308
We're going to start
the fight with Eteamon.

387
00:22:55,820 --> 00:22:57,820
Next time, Digimon Adventure.

388
00:22:58,340 --> 00:22:59,800
The name of NANOMON.

389
00:23:00,160 --> 00:23:02,480
Now, we're going to move on.
